{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/they-came-from/1464492-they-came-from\u2026-combat","id":1464492,"title":"They Came From\u2026 Combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","They Came From..."],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-19T03:29:22-07:00","id":1464492,"title":"They Came From\u2026 Combat","content":"I\u2019m reading <b>Beyond the Grave</b> and have some questions about combat in <b>They Came From</b> lines. I\u2019m familiarized with <b>Scion</b> version of Storypath that I run two years now. But here are my questions about <b>TCF</b> lines variant\u2026<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>They Came From</b> lines use \u2018double 10s\u2019, instead of \u2018exploding 10\u2019s of <b>Scion</b>.</li> <li>There is <b>no Defense</b> stat in at all, \u2018Defense\u2019 is always 1 ( Difficulty to hit attack ). By this, there is no <i>Extra Damage Stunt </i>to get next Health Damage level, only you burn 1:1 success on Damage. For example, when I have 3 success from attack and Enhancement from weapons, I generally do 2 Injuries for enemy? ( 3 Succs - 1 'always Defense' = 2 Injuries on hit ? )</li> <li>PCs have 10 Injury levels, de facto Health 10, with various damage levels giving bonuses. Health for antagonists and monsters in numeral, not the Injury levels like in <b>Scion</b>.</li> </ol>I get it right, for now? Those are major differences between <b>TCF </b>and <b>Scion</b> Storypath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-19-2021, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20